# The project's own docs corpus (project.md, architecture.md, and any
# src/*.md as they convert) is what this root is for. Everything below is
# a *separate* concern that happens to live in the same git repo and must
# not be swept into it just because this root now sits above them.

# Cargo's build output. Never content, reappears on every build.
/target/

# The test suite's own fixture corpora -- some deliberately carry broken
# links and stale eval results, since that is exactly what several tests
# assert dankg reports. Real content, for a different purpose than this
# root's.
/tests/

# Self-contained demo corpora, each already scoped by its own `.dankg/`
# for exactly this reason -- shown to a *user* getting started with dankg,
# not part of dankg's own design record.
/example/

# The self-hosting pilots, each deliberately scoped to its own `.dankg/`
# root already ("so this never touches the real crate's own corpus" --
# literate/hash.md's own config comment). Left excluded here for the same
# reason, now from the other direction.
/literate/
